{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>He was the one doing.</b> Targum explained: ״עַל מֵימְרֵיהּ״ (by his word). According to its own words, why does the verse not speak plainly and say explicitly ״עַל פִּיו הָיוּ עוֹשִׂים״ (by his word they would do)? Or perhaps the verse intended, by changing the expression, to convey also that although he was the one in charge, he did not conduct himself with authoritarianism and withhold himself from engaging in any task that the prisoners there would do, but his hand was equal to the hand of them all. And this tells of the temperament of his nature, that he is good and found favor and good understanding in the eyes of HaShem and man."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:10.793738342Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}